Ansible 2.19 introduced stricter Jinja sandbox restrictions that block previously working template expressions  including integer bitwise dunder methods (like `__or__`) and collection mutation methods (like `list.append`  `dict.update`). These methods were relied upon by users as the only way to perform certain operations in templates  but are now rejected as unsafe attributes even though they are safe operations. __or__ list.append list.extend dict.update _ANSIBLE_TEMPLAR_SANDBOX_MODE ansible -m debug -a msg='{{ (0x20).__or__(0xf) }}' localhost

{% set my_list = [] %}
{% set _ = my_list.append(1) %}
{{ my_list }}

{% set my_dict = {} %}
{% set _ = my_dict.update(a=1) %}
{{ my_dict }}

