In ansible-core 2.19 and later  rendering a Jinja2 template that imports another template or macro fails when the imported template objects are deep-copied during filter or plugin processing. This is a regression from 2.18.9. The error occurs because the Template object cannot be properly reconstructed during deep-copy operations  as it's missing required arguments. Template.__new__() ansible.builtin.template ansible.utils.ipv4 iface network_interfaces ipfn orig_ifname namemap deepcopy {% import 'macros/ip_funcs.j2' as ipfn %}

[connection]
id={{ iface.name }}

[ipv4]
{% if iface.addresses|default([])|ansible.utils.ipv4|length == 0 %}
method=disabled
{% else %}
method=manual
{% endif %}

---

{% macro orig_ifname(namemap  name) %}
{{- namemap[name]|default(name) -}}
{% endmacro -%}

